==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Canopy Queen Tomoe''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Canopy Queen Tomoe is a versatile crowd-controller/DPS hybrid, with applicability against a majority of her targets. Just like [[Ninja Girl Tomoe (Uber Rare Cat)|Ninja Girl Tomoe]], she has a two part [[Multi-Hit]] that aims to strike frontliners and backliners specifically. Although a majority of her damage is allocated to her first hit, its base DPS sits at a middling ~3,720 at Lv.30 (~5,907 at Lv.50), only brought up to ~6,695 with [[Strong Against]] (~10,634 at Lv.50). This flaw is somewhat made up for by her 50% chance to [[Freeze]] targets for 4 seconds; she attacks quickly, so enemies will be constantly reapplied with the effect. It is worth noting that her foreswing animation is quite long, so she can miss her attacks if enemies get displaced into her blind spot. Regardless, if she outranges a target, she counters them reliably, be it [[Berserkory]], [[Star Peng]], [[I.M. Phace]], [[Angelic Sleipnir]], [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]], or whatever else.

Where things get more interesting is in the face of [[Gauntlet|Colossus Gauntlets]], where she soft-counters the three associated with her target traits remarkably well. Tomoe outranges [[Baron Seal]], [[Archangel Exiel]], and [[Super Hyppoh]], and can fully utilize each of her knockbacks with the sheer bulk given to her by [[Colossus Slayer]] and Strong Against. [[Baron Seal Strikes/Red Alert 1~20|Red Alert Lv.11~20]], specifically, even features only enemies within her targets. The only Gauntlet that poses a problem to her is [[Horrorpotamus/Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.1~20|Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.11~20]], where [[Tackey]] can snipe her clean out of existence if you're not careful. All in all, Tomoe's time in the jungle has really paid dividents with how well-rounded she is.

